# Fixed defect 116 (panel 181, 2026-09-28). Symptom: `y = a +` over `1` at the
# statement's own margin compiled and printed 6, where design.md §4.15 reads
# *at bracket depth zero every line's indentation is structural: a long
# expression is broken inside parentheses or not at all*; one level deeper
# the same break was refused as a block. Cause: the lexer planted no
# terminator after a token that cannot end a line (Go's rule, panel 007), and
# the same margin planted no indent, so the statement went on. Now the line
# end is refused, once, and the fix writes the statement on one line.

record P
    x: i64

function main()
    a: i64 = 5
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    y = a +
    1
    print(y)
    p = P(x: 2)
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    n = p.
    x
    print(n)
